		Intel X86 BSP

Table of Contents
=================

	1. Supported Boards
	2. Change History
	3. BSP Notes

1. Supported Boards
===================

This BSP supports the following boards:

	- Intel Ice Lake-SP: 3rd Gen Intel(R) Xeon(R) Scalable processor
	- Intel Alder Lake N: Intel(R) Atom(TM) x7425E processor

2. Change History
=================

	- 2026/10 (LINUXPG-2901) Add Ice Lake-SP support
	- 2026/10 (LINUXPG-2936) Add Alder Lake N support

3. BSP Notes
============

This BSP has been validated exclusively for the boards listed in the following
'Validated Board Info' sections. Using it with other hardware configurations may
result in compatibility issues.

3.1 Intel Ice Lake-SP
---------------------

Ice Lake-SP is Intel's 3rd Generation of Xeon Scalable Processors which is
built on 10nm process, as the successor to Cascade Lake-SP.

3.1.1 Validated Board Info
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

[BIOS info]
	Vendor: Intel Corporation
	Version: SE5C6200.86B.4018.D65.2010201151
	Release Date: 10/20/2020

[Processor Info]
	Cpu family      : 6
	Model           : 106
	Model name      : Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8360Y CPU
	Stepping        : 6

[Board info]
	 Intel Server System M50CYP Family

3.1.2 Supported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	o Bus
		+ PCI Express 4.0
		+ I2C/SMBus: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family SMBus [8086:a1a3] (rev 0a)

	o Network
		+ Gb Ethernet: Intel Corporation I210 Gigabit Network Connection [8086:1533] (rev 03)
		+ 10Gb Ethernet: Intel Corporation Ethernet Controller 10G X550T [8086:1563] (rev 01)

	o USB
		+ USB 3.0 Host: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family USB 3.0 xHCI Controller [8086:a1af] (rev 0a)

	o Storage
		+ SATA3: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family SATA Controller [AHCI mode] [8086:a182] (rev 0a)

	o Multimedia
		+ Graphics: ASPEED Technology, Inc. ASPEED Graphics Family [1a03:2000] (rev 41)

	o Power Management
		+ CPU Freq: ACPI P-state
		+ CPU Idle: ACPI C-state
		+ ACPI S0
		+ ACPI S4

	o Misc Devices
		+ RTC: PC-style CMOS RTC
		+ Input device
			+ USB mouse & keyboard
		+ HW Monitor: Intel CPU core temperature sensor

	o NUMA (Non-Uniform Memory Access)

	o TPM2.0

	o EDAC

	o Intel Optane Persistent Memory 200 Series Module (Code name: Barlow Pass)

3.1.3 Unsupported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following features are not supported and not validated.

	x Hardware Watchdog
	x ACPI S3
	x Intel QuickAssist Adapter 8970

1) You can see the following log during kernel booting.

    iTCO_wdt: unable to reset NO_REBOOT flag, device disabled by hardware/BIOS.

This means the watchdog is disabled by HW/BIOS, and thus not usable.

2) ACPI S3 is not supported by BIOS.

3) Intel has not released QAT packages for kernel v6.18.

3.1.4 Notes
~~~~~~~~~~~

The default serial console port is ttyS1 at I/O 0x2f8. It may be different on your board
due to different hardware or BIOS settings.

3.2 Intel Alder Lake N
----------------------

Intel Atom processors x7000E Series feature the Efficient-core and Intel UHD Graphics
driven by Xe architecture as 12th Gen Intel Core processors.

3.2.1 Validated Board Info
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

[BIOS Info]
	Vendor: Intel Corporation
	Version: TWLNFWI1.R00.6491.A51.2512311039
	Release Date: 12/31/2025

[CPU Info]
	BIOS Model name:     Intel(R) Atom(TM) x7425E CPU
	BIOS CPU family:     43
	CPU family:          6
	Model:               190
	Thread(s) per core:  1
	Core(s) per socket:  4
	Socket(s):           1
	Stepping:            0

[Board Info]
	Alder Lake-N DDR5 CRB FAB A

3.2.2 Supported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	o Bus
		+ PCI-Express
		+ I2C/SMBus
			+ SMBus [0c05]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54a3]

	o Network
		+ Ethernet controller [0200]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54ac]
		+ Ethernet controller [0200]: Intel Corporation Ethernet Controller (2) I225-IT [8086:0d9f] (rev 03)
		+ WiFi & Bluetooth
			+ M.2 Key E: Intel Corporation Wi-Fi 6 AX210 with Bluetooth

	o USB (up to USB 3.2 Gen1)
		+ USB Host Mode
			+ USB controller [0c03]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:464e]
			+ USB controller [0c03]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54ed]
		+ USB Device Mode
			+ USB controller [0c03]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:465e]
			+ USB controller [0c03]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54ee]

	o Storage
		+ SATA
			+ SATA controller [0106]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54d3] (prog-if 01 [AHCI 1.0])
		+ MMC/SD
			+ SD Host controller [0805]: Intel Corporation Device [8086:54c4] (prog-if 01)
		+ NVME

	o Power Management
		+ CPU Freq: ACPI P-state
		+ CPU Idle: ACPI C-state
		+ ACPI S0
		+ ACPI S3
		+ ACPI S4

	o Multimedia
		+ Graphics: VGA compatible controller [0300]: Intel Corporation Alder Lake-N [UHD Graphics] [8086:46d1]
			+ DP
			+ HDMI
		+ Audio:
			+ Audio Codec - ALC245
			+ Audio via DP
			+ Audio via HDMI

	o Misc Devices
		+ UART: 8250/16550A compatible serial port
		+ Input device
			+ USB mouse & keyboard
		+ Watchdog: WDAT (Watchdog Action Table)

	o EDAC (Error Detection And Correction)

	o Intel RAPL (Running Average Power Limit)

3.2.3 Unsupported Feature
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following feature is not supported and not validated.

	x PCH TSN port 2.5G Link speed is not supported due to 1G PHY limitation.

3.2.4 Notes
~~~~~~~~~~~

1) Watchdog functionality requires TCO timer to be enabled in BIOS.

   Intel Advanced Menu → PCH-IO Configuration → Enable TCO Timer <Enabled>

2) The NVME port supports PCIe 3.0 x1 only due to hardware design constraints.

3) Recommended kernel parameters for the dump-capture kernel:

   nr_cpus=1 modprobe.blacklist=iwlwifi,cfg80211,intel_ish_ipc nomodeset intel_iommu=off

These parameters optimize crash kernel performance by limiting CPU usage to a single core, blacklisting
unnecessary wireless and sensor drivers, and disabling GPU and IOMMU initialization to prevent driver-related
hangs. The dump-capture kernel should be as simple as possible—minimizing complexity reduces the risk of
initialization failures and ensures reliable crash dump collection.
